.TH XNVME-PERF-XFER-HEAP 1 "24 November 2026" "xNVMe v0.8.1" "xNVMe"
.SH NAME
\fBxnvme-perf-xfer-heap \fP- Open the device with a host heap of each size of \fB--mib\fP and close it, once and then \fB--count\fP times, 100 by default. Report the microseconds of the first open and close apart, and the minimum, median and maximum of the \fB--count\fP after them. The upcie backends allocate the heap of hugetlb pages, lock it and map it for the device as they open it; XNVME_UPCIE_VFIO_MODE, iommufd or type1, chooses how they map it, and is printed. Other backends have no host heap.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.fam C
\fBxnvme-perf-xfer\fP \fIheap\fP <uri> [<args>]
.fam T
.fi
.fam T
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Open the device with a host \fIheap\fP of each size of \fB--mib\fP and close it, once and then \fB--count\fP times, 100 by default. Report the microseconds of the first open and close apart, and the minimum, median and maximum of the \fB--count\fP after them. The upcie backends allocate the \fIheap\fP of hugetlb pages, lock it and map it for the device as they open it; XNVME_UPCIE_VFIO_MODE, iommufd or type1, chooses how they map it, and is printed. Other backends have no host \fIheap\fP.
.SH REQUIRED
.TP
.B
<uri>
Device URI e.g. '/dev/nvme0n1', '0000:01:00.1', '10.9.8.1:8888', '\\.\PhysicalDrive1'
.TP
.B
\fB--mib\fP STRING
Sizes in MiB, separated by commas
.RE
.PP

.SH OPTIONAL
.TP
.B
[ \fB--count\fP NUM ]
Use given 'NUM' as count
.TP
.B
[ \fB--be\fP STRING ]
xNVMe backend, e.g. 'spdk', 'libvfn', 'upcie'
.TP
.B
[ \fB--homi-id\fP NUM ]
